presented globally by a Koszul-regular sequence of length `r`:

`⋀ⁱ_{O_X}(Ext¹_{O_Y}(O_X, O_X)) ⟶ Extⁱ_{O_Y}(O_X, O_X)`.

Three cases, and no two by the same argument. In negative degrees both sides vanish
(`isIso_extComparison_of_neg`). In degree zero both sides are free of rank one on their units,
and a homomorphism of graded algebras preserves the unit
(`isIso_extComparison_zero`). In positive degrees isomorphy is stalkwise and the stalk map is the
duality pairing between an exterior power of a free module and the exterior power of its dual,
read off from the local computation (`isIso_extComparison_of_pos`).

