local presentation of the ideal by a Koszul-regular sequence, and what follows is this statement.
The passage itself is not performed here, which is why this declaration is not registered under
the tag; the tag's local step, stated at the tag's own hypothesis, is in
`KoszulSelfExtExteriorLocal`, and its global statement, which carries the tag, is in
`KoszulSelfExtKoszulRegular` — see the implementation notes. -/
theorem isIso_extComparison_forall (i : ℤ) : IsIso (extComparison Rc K i) := by
  rcases lt_trichotomy i 0 with h | h | h
  · exact isIso_extComparison_of_neg Rc K h
  · subst h
    exact isIso_extComparison_zero Rc K
  · exact isIso_extComparison_of_pos Rc K h

/-- **The self-Ext algebra of a Koszul-regular quotient is an exterior algebra on its degree-one
piece**, for an ideal sheaf presented globally by a Koszul-regular sequence. The equivalent
formulation of `isIso_extComparison_forall`, by
`isExteriorAlgebra_extSelfAlgebra_of_isIso`. -/
theorem isExteriorAlgebra_extSelfAlgebra :
